.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-CHANGE-NAMESPACE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-change-namespace \- switch the active namespace for this session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eam change-namespace
.BR \-\-namespace | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Switches the namespace this session is restricted to. The server
validates that
.I NAME
exists under the caller's account, and that the caller either is an
account administrator or holds an explicit grant for it (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1));
otherwise the request is rejected and nothing local is changed.
.PP
On success, the namespace is persisted to
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
and is then sent as the
.I x\-euclid\-namespace
header on every subsequent command, in every module - not just eam - until
changed again with this command, cleared with an empty string, or
overwritten by a fresh
.B euclid-cli-eam-login (1)
that specifies its own
.BR \-\-namespace .
Only one namespace is active per session; there is no per-command
override.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-namespace " " \fINAME\fR
Namespace to make active. An empty string clears it, returning the
session to unscoped (the default before this command is ever run).
Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The namespace was validated (or cleared) and saved locally.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, the session
is not authenticated, the namespace does not exist, or access to it has
not been granted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam change-namespace \e
    --namespace production

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam change-namespace \e
    --namespace ""
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
Where the active namespace is persisted, alongside the session's bearer
token and SigV4 access key.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1)
